@startuml
title Queue Management Platform — ETA Sequence

actor Customer

participant "ETA Service" as ETA
participant "Queue" as Queue
participant "Ticket" as Ticket
participant "ServiceProviderService" as SPS

Customer -> ETA : Request ETA(ticket)

ETA -> Queue : Get operational position of target
Queue --> ETA : Tickets ahead + current service

note right of Queue
Operational order is determined by:
1. Priority group
2. Queue position

Only tickets ahead of the target contribute to the ETA.
end note

alt IN_SERVICE ticket exists

    Queue --> ETA : Current IN_SERVICE ticket

    ETA -> SPS : Get duration estimate\n(provider + service)
    SPS --> ETA : Estimated duration

    ETA -> Ticket : Get inServiceAt
    Ticket --> ETA : inServiceAt

    ETA -> ETA : Calculate elapsed duration
    ETA -> ETA : Remaining = max(estimated - elapsed, 0)

else No IN_SERVICE ticket

    ETA -> ETA : Current service remaining = 0

end

loop For each ticket ahead of target

    ETA -> Ticket : Get service
    Ticket --> ETA : Service

    ETA -> SPS : Get duration estimate\n(provider + service)
    SPS --> ETA : Estimated duration

    ETA -> ETA : Add estimated duration

end

ETA -> ETA : ETA = current remaining\n+ durations of tickets ahead

ETA --> Customer : Return derived ETA

note right of ETA
ETA is derived dynamically.
It is NOT persisted on Ticket.

Duration estimation:
< 3 completed valid services: use defaultDurationMinutes.
>= 3 completed valid services: use mean(actual durations).

Actual duration = completedAt - inServiceAt.

Historical durations are scoped to:
ServiceProvider + Service.

ETA does not modify:
position
priority
order
status
notifications.

ETA calculation does not require queue mutation.
end note

@enduml